## 5. Governance & Compliance Gateways

*Depending on the project track, the following non-negotiable standards must be validated prior to development or rollout.*

### 5.1 Track A & C Gateway: Digital Software Standards *(Governed by `AGENTS.md`)*
*For any initiative involving web applications, APIs, or database changes in the `jaipur-rugs` monorepo:*

- [ ] **One Singular Database:** Built entirely inside the shared Supabase project (`matnispbauvvlnbsuzxq`). No isolated per-app databases.
- [ ] **Data Model & Schema First:** Plain-language entities defined, Mermaid ERD (`.mmd`) placed in `db/<module>/`, reviewed before SQL is generated.
- [ ] **Strict Postgres Conventions:** UUID PKs (`id`), foreign keys (`<entity>_id`), `timestamptz created_at/updated_at`, Postgres `enum` for statuses (no arbitrary text).
- [ ] **Security Boundaries & RLS:** Row Level Security (RLS) policies written alongside schema. Helper functions placed in `private` schema (never `public`).
- [ ] **Zero Elevated Privileges in Apps:** No app or client code holds a Supabase `service-role key`. Frontend client is strictly read-only (`packages/supabase-client`).
- [ ] **Edge Functions for Writes:** All database writes executed via Supabase Edge Functions under `supabase/functions/<module>-<action>` and invoked through `packages/db-management-client`.
- [ ] **Unified Tech Stack:** Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Hero UI, Bklit Charts, pnpm workspaces + Turborepo. No secondary UI kits or charting tools.
- [ ] **Session & Access Control:** Auth cookies set to `.jaipurrugs.com` via `packages/auth`. Every app verifies role/department access independently on load.
- [ ] **Migration Ledger:** Every migration tested, linters/advisors checked, and documented in `db/MIGRATIONS.md`.

### 5.2 Track B & C Gateway: Operational & Physical Standards
*For physical processes, manufacturing changes, artisan workflows, and logistics:*

- [ ] **Standard Operating Procedure (SOP):** Formal step-by-step SOP written in Hindi & English, illustrated with visual diagrams for field staff.
- [ ] **Cross-Department SLA Sign-off:** Handoff protocols between impacted departments (e.g., Weaving Hub -> Quality Check -> Jaipur Warehouse) formally approved.
- [ ] **Artisan & Worker Safety/Welfare:** Verified that process modifications respect artisan working conditions, timely fair pay guarantees, and ergonomics.
- [ ] **Training & Enablement Plan:** Scheduled hands-on training sessions for branch staff, weavers, or dispatchers before live cutover.
- [ ] **Rollback / Contingency SOP:** Documented fallback procedure if operational equipment, power, or internet connectivity fails in rural centers.

